          "source": "Token Creation Logic",
          "heading": "Rules",
          "markdown": "1. **Raw values only in `_global`** — except `dimensions`, which holds its own numbers instead of pointing to `metrics/*` (kept simple on purpose). Name raw values by what they are, not where they're used.\n2. **`color` aliases `_global`.** Light/dark lives here.\n3. **Every surface gets an on-surface pair** for its text and icons.\n4. **States:** enabled, hover, pressed, disabled, loading.\n5. **`components` aliases `color` and `dimensions`.** Desktop/mobile lives here, never light/dark. Exceptions: `color/transparent`, and `metrics/*` for one-off sizes with no `dimensions` step. Missing something? Ask first.\n6. **Component tokens are lowercase and namespaced** by component. Multi-word properties are camelCase (`paddingX`, `cornerRadius`).\n7. **No component typography tokens.** Text binds the semantic `typography` tokens directly.\n8. **Never change how a component looks unless asked.** Keep radius, size, padding and colors as they are. A square stays square, even if it looks like a button. Don't guess from what a component \"looks like\" — copy what's there.\n9. **Every value gets a component token.** Colors, padding, gap, radius, stroke and sizes bind to a `components` token — never straight to `color`, `dimensions` or `_global`. Only text binds `typography` directly (rule 7). No raw numbers or hex left.\n10. **Check with code, not by eye.** Run the AI checks below every time. Work is not done until the audit returns `PASS`.\n11. **Interactive components follow [[Component Patterns]].** Hover = hard shadow (blur 0, spread 0, Y only), Y bound to `<component>/shape/shadowY`, color bound to the component's hover border token. Pressed = `stroke/m`, no shadow. Shadow size by component size: small controls `shadow-size/m`, controls `shadow-size/l`, containers `shadow-size/xl`. Read that note before building any interactive component. **Trigger:** when the user says a component should be interactive, follow \"Make it interactive\" in that note — add the states, tokens and hover shadow without being asked.\n\n### AI checks (run every time)\n\nReplace `NODE_ID` with the component (set) id, e.g. `14553:25234`. Run with `figma_execute`.\n\n**1. Snapshot — before any change.** Keep the result.\n\n```js\nconst root = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('NODE_ID');\nconst hex = c => '#' + [c.r, c.g, c.b].map(x => Math.round(x * 255).toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('');\nconst paints = a => Array.isArray(a) ? a.filter(p => p.visible !== false && p.type === 'SOLID').map(p => hex(p.color) + (p.opacity < 1 ? '@' + p.opacity : '')) : undefined;\nconst KEYS = ['width','height','paddingLeft','paddingRight','paddingTop','paddingBottom','itemSpacing','topLeftRadius','topRightRadius','bottomLeftRadius','bottomRightRadius','strokeWeight','fontSize'];\nconst out = {};\nfunction walk(n, path) {\n  const p = path ? path + ' > ' + n.name : n.name;\n  const s = {};\n  for (const k of KEYS) if (typeof n[k] === 'number') s[k] = Math.round(n[k] * 100) / 100;\n  s.fills = paints(n.fills); s.strokes = paints(n.strokes);\n  out[n.id + ' ' + p] = s;\n  if ('children' in n && n.type !== 'INSTANCE') n.children.forEach(c => walk(c, p));\n}\nwalk(root, '');\nreturn out;\n```\n\n**2. Snapshot again — after the changes.** Compare with step 1. Any difference that isn't in the approved plan → revert it.\n\n**3. Audit — must return `PASS`.** Anything listed → fix and run again. After 3 rounds, report what's left and stop.\n\n```js\nconst root = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('NODE_ID');\nconst cols = await figma.variables.getLocalVariableCollectionsAsync();\nconst colName = Object.fromEntries(cols.map(c => [c.id, c.name]));\nconst issues = [];\nasync function check(n, field, alias, want) {\n  if (!alias) { issues.push(`${n.name} › ${field}: raw value`); return; }\n  const v = await figma.variables.getVariableByIdAsync(alias.id);\n  const col = v ? (colName[v.variableCollectionId] ?? 'library') : 'missing';\n  if (col !== want) issues.push(`${n.name} › ${field}: bound to ${col}/${v?.name}, should be ${want}`);\n}\nconst PAD = ['paddingLeft','paddingRight','paddingTop','paddingBottom'];\nconst RAD = ['topLeftRadius','topRightRadius','bottomLeftRadius','bottomRightRadius'];\nconst TXT = ['fontFamily','fontStyle','fontSize','lineHeight','letterSpacing'];\nasync function walk(n) {\n  if (n.type !== 'COMPONENT_SET') {\n    const b = n.boundVariables || {};\n    const auto = n.layoutMode && n.layoutMode !== 'NONE';\n    if (auto) for (const k of PAD) if (n[k] > 0) await check(n, k, b[k], 'components');\n    if (auto && n.itemSpacing > 0 && n.primaryAxisAlignItems !== 'SPACE_BETWEEN') await check(n, 'itemSpacing', b.itemSpacing, 'components');\n    for (const k of RAD) if (n[k] > 0) await check(n, k, b[k], 'components');\n    const hasStroke = Array.isArray(n.strokes) && n.strokes.some(s => s.visible !== false);\n    if (hasStroke && typeof n.strokeWeight === 'number' && n.strokeWeight > 0) await check(n, 'strokeWeight', b.strokeWeight, 'components');\n    for (const key of ['fills','strokes']) if (Array.isArray(n[key])) for (const p of n[key]) if (p.visible !== false && p.type === 'SOLID') await check(n, key, p.boundVariables?.color, 'components');\n    if (n.type === 'TEXT') for (const k of TXT) { const a = b[k]; await check(n, k, Array.isArray(a) ? a[0] : a, 'typography'); }\n  }\n  if ('children' in n && n.type !== 'INSTANCE') for (const c of n.children) await walk(c);\n}\nawait walk(root);\nreturn issues.length ? issues : 'PASS';\n```\n\nNot checked on purpose: values of 0, the component set's own frame, and anything inside nested instances (they're checked in their own component)."
